pr</td></tr><tr><td>5: Protected Areas and Wildlife</td><td>Nepal protects its biodiversity through 10 national parks (Chitwan, Bardia, Banke, Shuklaphanta, Koshi Tappu, Parsa, Ranipurna, Sagarmatha, Langtang, Annapurna, Makalu), 6 conservation areas (Kanchenjunga, Manaslu, etc.), 1 hunting reserve, and Ramsar wetlands. Chitwan (1973) and Sagarmatha (1976) are UNESCO World Heritage Sites. The IUCN Red List (EX, EW, CR, EN, VU, NT, LC) tracks species risk; in Nepal, the Bengal tiger (EN), one-horned rhino (VU), snow leopard (VU), and Asian elephant (EN) are key endangered species. Threats include habitat loss, poaching, pollution, and climate change. Conservation strategies (in-situ, ex-situ, community forestry, anti-poaching, CITES) are essential to prevent extinction. NEB focuses on protected areas, IUCN categories, endangered species, causes of extinction, and conservation strategies.</td></tr><tr><td>6: Wildlife: Importance, Causes of Extinction and Conservation Strategies</td><td>Wildlife underpins ecosystem function and human well-being, yet faces severe threats from habitat loss, overexploitation, invasive species, and climate change. Effective conservation combines legal frameworks, protected areas, captive breeding, and community engagement.</td></tr><tr><td>7: IUCN Categories of Threatened Species</td><td>The IUCN Red List uses standardized categories (EX, EW, CR, EN, VU, NT, LC, DD, NE) to assess extinction risk. Understanding these categories is essential for prioritizing conservation action and policy.</td></tr><tr><td>8: Endangered Species in Nepal</td><td>Nepal's endangered species — including rhino, tiger, snow leopard, red panda, and gharial — reflect both severe threats and successful recovery efforts. Protected areas, anti-poaching, community forestry, and international cooperation have driven notable conservation successes.</td></tr></table><h2>Diagrams</h2><h3>IUCN Red List categories</h3><img src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/IUCN_Red_List.svg/800px-IUCN_Red_List.svg.png" alt="IUCN Red List categories" style="max-width:100%"><br><h3>IUCN Protected Areas</h3><img src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/IUCN_Protected_Areas.svg/800px-IUCN_Protected_Areas.svg.png" alt="IUCN Protected Areas" style="max-width:100%"><br></body></html>